        "How often do I actually need to check my budget?",
        `You do not need to stare at it all day. Check it at moments when the information can change a decision—especially before flexible or unplanned spending and when something meaningful changes in the cycle.\n\nThe purpose is to connect the plan to behavior. If you only review the budget after everything is spent, it becomes a report instead of a guide.\n\nA short check before a decision can be more valuable than a long review after the money is gone.`
